==> chunking is split into 2 parts:

1- lexical:
this is where the split based on number of characters or tokens, commas, sentences, markdown actions
basically lexical is about splitting based on an sliding window chunking

2- semantic:
based on meaning
semantic chunking finds the meaning by using embedding to detect changes in meanign
it compares the vector next to it, to compare with the current vector, to see if they are clsoe in meaning

lexical: faster, doesnt understand topics boundaries
semantic: slower, does understand topics boundaries

using an AI Agent to troubleshoot something, its better to have a rag based on semantic chunking
chunking logs for example, is better to have it done in semantic 
to keep the conexts of logs intact!



